     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Ashly Romero<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, August 11, 2023 11:55 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Separate fixed and semi-landmark files, need combining?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi all,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">A student placed fixed landmarks and semi-landmarks on macaque specimens in 3D Slicer and exported the files as .json. For each specimen, they gave me one fixed landmark .json file and one semi-landmark.json file. My understanding from\r\n previous work is that all landmarks for a specimen have to be in the same file to be able to use gpagen in geomorph. Is that correct? If so, how can I combine these files for each specimen when I read them into R? Or maybe it’s possible to combine them in\r\n 3D Slicer before exporting so that I can use them with the geomorph functions? Any ideas are much appreciated! I’d hate for them to have to redo any data collection.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">All the best,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Ashly<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<d